closeout-lint and hygiene-lint (both shimmed at ~/.local/bin) are broken today, found 2026-08-05 during a senechal /cloture run: closeout-lint's section A FLAGs EVERY registered repo (including senechal, baudin, scheduler, realisateur itself) as [missing-repo] '$HOME/Documents/Projects/<name> does not exist', even though `ls /home/zach/Documents/Projects/` shows all of them present and `cd`-able. hygiene-lint senechal similarly reports '(no git repo at that path -- skipped)' for a path that unambiguously has a live .git and an open PR (#28) against it. Both tools apparently resolve project paths through something other than a plain $HOME/Documents/Projects/<name> check (a stale registry file, a cached realpath, a case/symlink mismatch -- not diagnosed further, out of senechal's domain to fix). Also noted in the same run: hygiene-lint's section 10 flags /bashify, /cloture, /ideate shims as drifted from source (rerun bin/install-shims.sh) -- may be the same root cause or unrelated, worth checking together. Filed rather than fixed per the delegation model; senechal owns noticing, realisateur owns its own tooling.
